{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks","id":1333332,"title":"On masquerade breaks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-30T18:19:04-07:00","id":1333332,"title":"On masquerade breaks","content":"So here's the thing. No one knows about it, right? No one. No one knows about magic, the haemophages, the shapeshifters, etc.... So I got an idea. A city is taken by the Nephandi in a massive ritual as ritual sacrifice. They're not being killed, of course, not directly. But they are certainly affected, and so an entire city is taken, and thrown through the Gauntlet itself. <br /> <br /> Within the city, there are:<ul><li>Changelings</li> <li>Werewolves</li> <li>Vampires</li> <li>Traditions</li> <li>Technocrats</li> </ul><br /> So now, they all have to make sure that the people of the city do not die horribly to the things lurking in the spiritual realm (this counts as sacrifices). A city's worth of sacrifices, can summon seriously bad juju, and the predators that seek to devour the city's inhabitants gain strength the more people they consume. <br /> <br /> Can they protect these people? Can they find their way back to the other side of the Gauntlet? Can they do this, without tearing each other to pieces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T22:14:42-07:00","id":1333351,"title":"","content":"In short. Yes. A cities worth of people would form a Pericarp fairly rapidly as their collective consensus formatted the Umbra into just another section of realspace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T22:35:22-07:00","id":1333352,"title":"","content":"No, because humans cease to be human in the Umbra after about a month and a half. The question is can they get the city back in that time frame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T11:50:46-07:00","id":1333414,"title":"","content":"M20 says it's about Three months.<br /> <br /> Which is still rather short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T12:03:49-07:00","id":1333418,"title":"","content":"If... a group (hopefully a group) of Nephandi are powerful enough to literally toss a whole city into the Umbra? It all seems kinda moot since the world is truly and utterly fucked at that point.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible to save the people, especially for the Technocracy (NWO agents to run the evacuation, VEs to handle transport), but undoing the city itself being gone is a lost cause.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T05:46:16-07:00","id":1333512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1333418#post1333418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If... a group (hopefully a group) of Nephandi are powerful enough to literally toss a whole city into the Umbra? It all seems kinda moot since the world is truly and utterly fucked at that point.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible to save the people, especially for the Technocracy (NWO agents to run the evacuation, VEs to handle transport), but undoing the city itself being gone is a lost cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That is true. Maybe this city throwing is the first shot, and the technocracy and any other supernatural being is currently busy fighting them, forcing them to go it alone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T05:49:03-07:00","id":1333513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1333351#post1333351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short. Yes. A cities worth of people would form a Pericarp fairly rapidly as their collective consensus formatted the Umbra into just another section of realspace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that sucks. Was hoping for an interesting story where they're trying to shepherd a city's worth of humanity to safety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T19:51:33-07:00","id":1333630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1333513#post1333513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow that sucks. Was hoping for an interesting story where they're trying to shepherd a city's worth of humanity to safety.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How big a city does it need to be? You could always pull the plot of Robotech/Macross...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T23:21:41-07:00","id":1333642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1333630#post1333630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How big a city does it need to be? You could always pull the plot of Robotech/Macross...</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of plot? Maybe this is too big. Maybe a chantry and a construct, and a school for fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T05:31:03-07:00","id":1333654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1333642#post1333642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of plot? Maybe this is too big. Maybe a chantry and a construct, and a school for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Macross/robotech has a human starship basically get attacked by Aliens when its first getting out there so they use a space fold drive that leaves them on the far side of the solar system with the CITY beneath the ship and the end up having to incorporate it into the spaceship and deal with civilians etc.<br /> <br /> I think you could take something from that some sort of Plot point that causes the Technocrats and others to be on the far Side of the solar system, which is deep into various inhuman creatures territory and having to shepherd/conrol the population. I wouldn't put a hephandi in charge though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T00:40:50-07:00","id":1335271,"title":"","content":"Weird at last! Weird at last!<br /> God Almighty, weird at last!<br /> <i>Welcome to Nightvale....</i><br /> <br /> <br /> We are living in an immaterial world, a ghost world, and I am an immaterial girl - a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Cecil made me do it. 09-12-2019, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T00:48:46-07:00","id":1335272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1335271#post1335271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Welcome to Nightvale....</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T00:48:46-07:00","id":1335273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1333332-on-masquerade-breaks?p=1335271#post1335271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Welcome to Nightvale....</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T01:01:58-07:00","id":1335276,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Welcome to Night Vale</b></i> is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Podcast\" target=\"_blank\">podcast</a> presented as a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radio_show\" target=\"_blank\">radio show</a> for the fictional town of Night Vale, reporting on the strange events that occur within it. The series was created in 2012 by Joseph Fink and Jeffrey Cranor. Published by Night Vale Presents since March 15, 2015,<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welcome_to_Night_Vale#cite_note-4\" target=\"_blank\">[4]</a></sup> the podcast was previously published by Commonplace Books.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welcome_to_Night_Vale#cite_note-5\" target=\"_blank\">[5]</a></sup> Cecil Gershwin Palmer\u2014the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radio_personality\" target=\"_blank\">host</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protagonist\" target=\"_blank\">main character</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First-person_narrative\" target=\"_blank\">narrator</a>\u2014is voiced by Cecil Baldwin, while secondary characters are sometimes voiced by guest stars\u2014such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dylan_Marron\" target=\"_blank\">Dylan Marron</a>, who voices Carlos. The podcast typically airs on the first and fifteenth of every month, and consists of &quot;news, announcements and advertisements&quot; from the desert town,<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welcome_to_Night_Vale#cite_note-Wynn-6\" target=\"_blank\">[6]</a></sup> located &quot;somewhere in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwestern_United_States\" target=\"_blank\">Southwestern United States</a>.&quot;<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welcome_to_Night_Vale#cite_note-D&#39;Amico-7\" target=\"_blank\">[7]</a></sup> In an interview with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPR\" target=\"_blank\">NPR</a>, Joseph Fink said that he &quot;came up with this idea of a town in that desert where all conspiracy theories were real, and we would just go from there with that understood.&quot;<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welcome_to_Night_Vale#cite_note-8\" target=\"_blank\">[8]</a></sup><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T01:05:15-07:00","id":1335278,"title":"","content":"Welcome to Night Vale is a podcast presented as a radio show for the fictional town of Night Vale, reporting on the strange events that occur within it. The series was created in 2012 by Joseph Fink and Jeffrey Cranor. Published by Night Vale Presents since March 15, 2015, the podcast was previously published by Commonplace Books. Cecil Gershwin Palmer\u2014the host, main character, and narrator\u2014is voiced by Cecil Baldwin, while secondary characters are sometimes voiced by guest stars\u2014such as Dylan Marron, who voices Carlos. The podcast typically airs on the first and fifteenth of every month, and consists of &quot;news, announcements and advertisements&quot; from the desert town, located &quot;somewhere in the Southwestern United States.&quot; In an interview with NPR, Joseph Fink said that he &quot;came up with this idea of a town in that desert where all conspiracy theories were real, and we would just go from there with that understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}